data/frequency.txt, usage-tags.txt, usage-ngrams.bin.gz, usage-pairs.txt,
usage-pairs.bin.gz and usage-countable.txt are counts made by tools/mkusage
over five English corpora of the Leipzig Corpora Collection (Wortschatz,
Universitaet Leipzig), one million sentences each:

    eng_news_2016_1M
    eng_news_2020_1M
    eng_news_2023_1M
    eng_wikipedia_2016_1M
    eng-com_web-public_2018_1M

    https://wortschatz.uni-leipzig.de/en/download/English

None of the text is in this repository or in the plugin. What ships is how
often words were found, and found beside one another: word frequencies, the
contexts of the words in data/confusion-sets.txt, which pairs of common words
were never adjacent, and which nouns were never without an article.

The collection asks to be cited as:

    D. Goldhahn, T. Eckart and U. Quasthoff. Building Large Monolingual
    Dictionaries at the Leipzig Corpora Collection: From 100 to 200 Languages.
    Proceedings of the 8th International Language Resources and Evaluation
    Conference (LREC'12), 2012.

LICENCE TO BE CONFIRMED. The collection's terms of use are at

    https://wortschatz.uni-leipzig.de/en/usage

and were not readable when these counts were made (the page sits behind a
browser check). They must be read, and this file completed with the licence
they state, before these files are redistributed. If the terms do not allow
it, tools/mkusage runs over any one-sentence-per-line English text and the
counts can be remade from another source.
